WHAT THIS REPOSITORY IS

The source for `virp-verify`, the standalone verifier for VIRP evidence
bundles, and for `docket-bundle`, the library it reads them with. These two
crates are published so that anyone handed a `virp-verify` binary can build
their own from source and compare hashes, rather than taking a stranger's
executable on trust. That is the entire reason this tree is public.

It is the release source: the binaries published as `virp-verify` releases are
built from this repository, at the tag named in the release.

WHAT THIS REPOSITORY IS NOT

It is not the whole of Docket. The bundle exporter, the report engine, the
redaction layer and the operational tooling live in a separate, private
repository. Nothing in this tree signs anything, holds a private key, or
executes anything from a bundle; the verifier is a pure reader by design, and
that is why it is the part that can be public.

`docket-bundle` keeps its name because "Docket" names the evidence-bundle
FORMAT this code parses, not a brand applied to it: `docket-bundle/0.1` and
`docket-report/0.8` are version strings inside every manifest and every report
this verifier reads and writes.

THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES

Every crate this tree links is listed in `Cargo.lock` and constrained by
`deny.toml`, which permits only MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD / Unicode / Zlib
licensed dependencies. Their notices remain with them.
